    "body": "fix on issue/672-plasma-laws-2 · PR #791 (draft, from mkinney:issue/672-plasma-laws-2, fork synced at v0.16.0) · pinned by sim `plasma_laws` (15) and `plasma_program` (5), motion `plasma::tests::a_slot_narrower_than_the_kerf_is_refused_not_bridged`, app `plasma_gate` (4), `plasma_machine`, `plasma_profile`, `post_not_judged` · merges at the next cut (feat).\n\nStep 2 done: `PlasmaProgram::from_toolpath` reads the laws' input from the torch records; `posting::plasma_clause` runs inside `verification_report`, so a plasma refusal blocks the post by name on every surface and the not-judged line says the 3D stock sim does not run for plasma (verdict = the 2D laws, clean or the warnings named); cut crossing (ring through an earlier ring) refuses; enclosure is recomputed from the rings and a disagreeing PARENT is refused; the step-1 review notes are in (small only on INNER, one-point cut pinned, open parent malformed); #676's item 12 is the generator's cover law (a slot, notch or keyway narrower than the kerf is refused, not bridged); #674's check note names where the through-cut is judged. Every refusal was shown load-bearing by removing it and watching its test fail (table in the PR). Linux batch gate running; result to follow on the PR. Label swap claimed -> in-review is the maintainer's (label edits are denied from this account).",
